  "task": "Prepare the monthly executive sales report. I need a clean, print-ready summary page showing: total revenue vs target, top 5 deals closed, and a regional breakdown with a mini bar chart. Merge header cells, apply professional formatting with the company color scheme (dark blue headers, white text), and set up print headers with the report date. The file to work on is /home/user/calc_sales_report_executive_043_initial.xlsx.\n\nRequirements (every item is checked; work on the existing sheet ExecReport):\n1. Title: merge A1:D1; the title cell is bold, font size at least 14 pt, white text (#FFFFFF) on a solid dark blue fill of exactly #1F3864.\n2. Revenue vs target: B5 (\"vs Target\") is a formula computing (Total Revenue - Monthly Target) / Monthly Target from B3 and B4, e.g. =(B3-B4)/B4 (any equivalent formula referencing B3 and B4 is fine; result 6.25%), formatted as a percentage.\n3. Currency: B3, B4 and the deal values (C8:C12) use a dollar currency number format (the format code contains \"$\").\n4. Section header rows 3, 7 and 14: bold, white text (#FFFFFF) on a solid fill of exactly #1F3864 (at least in column A of each of these rows; apply it across A:D).\n5. Insert a bar chart of the regional data (Region / Revenue / Target in A14:C18) on the ExecReport sheet; it must be the first chart on the sheet.\n6. Page setup: the page header contains the report title/date (e.g. the &D date field), and the page footer contains a page number (&P or the word \"Page\").\n7. Save the workbook in place at the same path, keeping the .xlsx format.",
